The fresh non-vacuity gate behaves correctly: the mutation parses (`--dry-run` exit 0) and the proof fails with `WarnStuckClaimState`, exposing the impossible obligation `absInt(A) + 2 = absInt(A)`. A separate terminating body mutation (`remainder = 0`) also parses and fails on the expected wrong-result residual. I’m consolidating the trust ledger and verdict now; the only material limitation is the trusted canonical’s negative-sign behavior conflicting with the ordinary non-negative GCD contract that the candidate proves.
The reviewer-authored false result and terminating body mutations both built and failed for the expected unmet obligations. Writing the final seven-stage review and trust accounting.
  ✓ Read required Kit skill instructions
  ✓ Stage 1: verify input, provenance, and supplied-semantics integrity
  ✓ Stage 2: check program fidelity and run independent differential tests
  ✓ Stage 3: rebuild definitions and reconstruct every positive proof
  ✓ Stage 4: audit adequacy and real-program pinning
